    {
      "text": "if ye salute your brethren only, what do ye more, Matt. 5:47. his brethren stood without, Matt. 12:46 (Mark 3:31; Luke 8:19). his brethren, James, and Joses, and Simon, and Judas, Matt. 13:55. were with us seven brethren, Matt. 22:25 (Mark 12:20; Luke 20:29). for one is your Master, even Christ; and all ye are brethren, Matt. 23:8. unto one of the least of these my brethren, Matt. 25:40. when thou art converted, strengthen thy brethren, Luke 22:32. neither did his brethren believe in him, John 7:5. continued with one accord in prayer … with his brethren, Acts 1:14. to visit his brethren the children of Israel, Acts 7:23 (15:36). relief unto the brethren which dwelt in Judæa, Acts 11:29. he might be the firstborn among many brethren, Rom. 8:29. when ye sin so against the brethren, 1 Cor. 8:12. Have we not power to lead about … the brethren of the Lord, 1 Cor. 9:5. he was seen of above five hundred brethren, 1 Cor. 15:6. this epistle be read unto all the holy brethren, 1 Thes. 5:27. entreat him as a father; and the younger men as brethren, 1 Tim. 5:1. not despise them, because they are brethren, 1 Tim. 6:2. he is not ashamed to call them brethren, Heb. 2:11. to be made like unto his brethren, Heb. 2:17. be ye all of one mind, having … love as brethren, 1 Pet. 3:8. death unto life, because we love the brethren, 1 Jn. 3:14. we ought to lay down our lives for the brethren, 1 Jn. 3:16. thou doest faithfully whatsoever thou doest to the brethren, 3 Jn. 1:5. for the accuser of our brethren is cast down, Rev. 12:10. thy brethren that have the testimony of Jesus, Rev. 19:10. am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren the prophets, Rev. 22:9.",
